course: dictionary
lesson: 10471
title: Tumble: falling, rolling and dropping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Young pandas really tumble and roll.» Tumble is a verb, and it can mean rolling over and over, the way a playful panda rolls about on the grass. The clues are the words roll and really, which show it is fun and lively.
explain: Tumble can also mean a fall. «Mole comes tumbling in, very pleased with himself.» Here Mole is not falling over. He is rushing in quickly and happily, so tumbling means moving in a fast, eager way. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Tumble has more than one meaning, so context decides which one you need. «A penny dropped from a skyscraper slows down in the air and tumbles.» The penny is falling and turning over as it drops. A tumble is a fall, so the words take a tumble and tumble down are useful to know too.
fact: To tumble means to fall down suddenly, often rolling over.
fact: To tumble also means to roll or turn over and over, as in gymnastics.
fact: To tumble can mean to drop quickly, like prices tumbling.
fact: A tumble is a fall, so you can take a tumble on the stairs.
fact: Phrases with tumble include «tumble down», «tumble dryer» and «rough and tumble».
exercise: «Young pandas really tumble and roll.» What does tumble mean here? | To sit very still | To eat slowly | *To roll or turn over and over | To write neatly
exercise: «Mole comes tumbling in, very pleased with himself.» What does tumbling suggest? | Walking in very slowly | Leaving the room sadly | *Rushing in quickly and eagerly | Crying loudly
exercise: What is a tumble? | A machine for drying clothes | A kind of cake | A big wave on the sea | *A fall
test: «The prices of the shares tumbled overnight.» What does tumbled mean here? | Stayed exactly the same | Were painted red | *Dropped quickly | Rose slowly
test: The toddler took a tumble on the stairs, so the family put up a stair gate. What is a tumble here? | A staircase | A rough game with friends | A gate | *A fall
exam: Which sentence uses tumble to mean roll or turn over and over? | «The sun was warm on the beach.» | «The shop was open late on Friday.» | «She wrote her name very neatly.» | *«The clothes went tumbling round in the dryer.»
